  "pin24ThreatTitle": "Threat model & recovery checklist",
  "pin24ThreatProtectsTitle": "What this screen does to protect the seed",
  "pin24ThreatProtectsBody": "• The seed field is always masked and never shown as plain text; you can paste into it, never copy out of it.\n• Keyboard suggestions, autocorrect, keyboard learning and autofill are off for the secret fields.\n• Everything is computed on this phone, offline, in a separate, short-lived background worker; nothing is sent to your Vaultwarden server, Firebase or anywhere else.\n• Nothing secret is saved: not in settings, cloud sync, backups or logs.\n• The derived seed stays in memory only to avoid re-deriving it, and is zeroed on “Wipe seed” and “Wipe all”, when you leave the PIN tab, when the app goes to the background, after 2 minutes without activity, and when the app locks.\n• Android blocks screenshots and recording of this tab; iOS hides it while the screen is recorded or mirrored.",
  "pin24ThreatCannotTitle": "What it CANNOT protect against",
  "pin24ThreatCannotBody": "• A compromised phone: malware, a jailbreak or root, or a malicious keyboard app (Android cannot block third-party keyboards; iOS forces the system keyboard in masked fields only).\n• Accessibility services and screen readers that can read the screen.\n• Screenshots on iOS (they cannot be blocked — you only get a warning), cameras and people looking over your shoulder.\n• Dart strings cannot be wiped: the phrase you typed may stay in app memory until it is overwritten. Only the binary seed buffers are zeroed.\n• Your memory: one wrong word gives a completely different PIN, and the checksum catches most mistakes but not all. A forgotten passphrase cannot be recovered.",
  "pin24ThreatUseTitle": "Use this tool when",
  "pin24ThreatUseBody": "• Your Ledger is lost, broken or out of reach and you need a PIN or password now.\n• You are about to restore the seed onto a new device anyway.",
  "pin24ThreatDontTitle": "Do NOT use it when",
  "pin24ThreatDontBody": "• The Ledger is available — use the device.\n• The phone is not yours, is jailbroken or rooted, or has unknown keyboard or accessibility apps.\n• Someone could be recording or watching the screen.\n• You just want convenience: typing the seed into a phone exposes it far more than the hardware wallet does.",
  "pin24ThreatStepsTitle": "Steps for a real recovery",
  "pin24ThreatStepsBody": "1. Use a phone you trust, ideally in airplane mode.\n2. Enter the passphrase too if you set one on the Ledger.\n3. Type the nickname exactly as on the device (case-sensitive).\n4. Derive what you need, copy or write it down, then press “Wipe all” and close the app from the app switcher.\n5. Restore the Ledger onto new hardware, and rotate especially valuable secrets if the phone may be compromised.",
  "pin24CleanupTitle": "Post-recovery cleanup",
  "pin24CleanupCaption": "When you are done: copy or write down what you need, press “Wipe all”, then close the app from the app switcher. Dart strings cannot be zeroed, so closing the app is what finally drops them from memory.",
